{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if his hand does not reach.</b> For the hand is what does labor, and it is what acquires — an allusion to one who does not have." "<b>One for a sin-offering and one for a burnt-offering.</b> Rav Isaac said that the reason for 'one burnt-offering' is because his hand did not reach — perhaps a thought arose in his mind. But what seems close to me is that the one corresponds to what was stated [i.e., the sin-offering], and the second is the burnt-offering according to its rule."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:39.329692496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}